"intro": "Use $1\\text{ kg}=1000\\text{ g}$ to convert masses between kilograms and grams.",
"facts": [
"$1\\text{ kg} = 1000\\text{ g}$, so $1\\text{ g} = \\tfrac{1}{1000}\\text{ kg} = 0.001\\text{ kg}$.",
"$500\\text{ g} = 0.5\\text{ kg}$, $250\\text{ g} = 0.25\\text{ kg}$, $750\\text{ g} = 0.75\\text{ kg}$.",
"Grams are smaller units than kilograms. Multiply by $1000$ to convert kilograms to grams; divide by $1000$ to convert grams to kilograms."
],
"steps": [
